{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"bairnly-elliptic-toad","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\n\nRunning rebar's provider seam emits, on every OpenAI-compatible build:\n\n```\nPydanticAIDeprecationWarning: In v2.0, 'openai:' will resolve to the OpenAI Responses API by\ndefault. Use 'openai-chat:' to keep current Chat Completions behavior, or 'openai-responses:'\nto opt in early.\n```\n\nSurfaced by the `7e9e-07f7-8fe1-4e38` spike that drove `ProviderSession.model_for(\"openai:...\")`.\nrebar's OpenAI-compatible builder is Chat-only by design (`_RebarOpenAICompatibleProvider`\nwithdraws `supports_json_schema_output` precisely because an opaque endpoint need not implement\nstrict `json_schema` decoding), so a silent switch to the Responses API at the v2.0 upgrade would\nchange the wire format under a gateway deployment that was working.\n\n`pyproject.toml` pins `pydantic-ai-slim>=1.107,<2`, so this is latent rather than live — but the\npin is the only thing holding it, and the fix is cheap now.\n\n## Approach\n\nEmit `openai-chat:` rather than bare `openai:` where rebar composes the provider-qualified model\nstring, so the intent is explicit and survives the v2.0 default flip. `openai-chat` is already a\nregistered builder name in `ProviderSession`, and `providers.py` already documents\n`openai-responses` as a name pydantic-ai resolves but rebar registers no builder for — so this\nchange states what rebar already does rather than altering behaviour.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/llm/config.py` — the `_PROVIDER_PREFIXES` entry that maps `gpt-*` to a provider.\n- `src/rebar/llm/providers.py` — the builder registration comment, if the name changes.\n- `tests/unit/test_provider_qualifier.py` — the existing invariant test over the table.\n\n## Testing\n\nTier: in-process unit tests against the real qualifier — pure string mapping.\n\n- Happy path: a `gpt-*` model qualifies to `openai-chat:`, and the result is a name\n  `ProviderSession.is_resolvable` accepts.\n- Regression: the existing whole-table invariant still holds for every other prefix.\n- No-warning: building an OpenAI-compatible provider emits no `PydanticAIDeprecationWarning`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A bare `gpt-4o` qualifies to `openai-chat:gpt-4o`; checked by asserting the qualifier's\n      output.\n- [ ] Building a provider for that qualified name emits no `PydanticAIDeprecationWarning`;\n      checked with `pytest.warns(None)`-style capture around the build.\n- [ ] The existing `test_provider_qualifier.py` whole-table invariant passes unchanged.","id":"b735-788d-72eb-411f","parent_id":"","priority":3,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Emit openai-chat: instead of bare openai: before the pydantic-ai v2.0 default flip"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787771620528237001,"uuid":"3229a73d-1ec9-479c-ac61-81038c8a2bf5"}